cmd: env
args: -i =x
timeout: 10
source: github.com/unixwin/WinuxCmd/issues/1462
tags: audit-w3b env empty-name-assignment accepted
# glibc putenv() performs no name validation, so coreutils env accepts an
# empty-name assignment and prints it like any other entry ("=x", exit 0).
# The original shape (`env '=x' printenv`) compared a full environment
# dump, which the interop launch can never byte-match (the Windows subject
# cannot receive the WSL side's variables, and a Windows child block
# cannot carry an empty-name entry at all); -i isolates the assignment as
# the entire comparable output.
